y $3$ coumns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns, while the matrix $A$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=4$ and $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $C.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321043 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c38e2b1e-6c94-5624-8794-4c613a255924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467310} {:answer/id #uuid "5d54ebf0-003a-5f1c-bd7e-8c9967853943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467311}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467310} :answer-field/id #uuid "e26dd5b4-e353-584a-b82f-a7001a7ceafd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80281206-d511-56fb-abc8-2ec2bd14982e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467312} {:answer/id #uuid "0ee50a33-bcd1-57ca-af8a-fea5667b18e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467312} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb96f6f-4c8d-5ec7-a8ea-8d4572cc6d20" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9723544-78fc-5712-9c8f-ca9dda43b954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467314} {:answer/id #uuid "c1730f02-53e8-5c11-881b-06d6506cf09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467315}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467315} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a295ee6-c8e9-5be1-8d44-50156c244fcb" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "43599508-ddd2-50d6-b640-692e29bcfb0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35283" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $6?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $6$ must have at least $6$ columns and at least $6$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $A$ since it has only $5$ columns and the matrix $B$ since it has only $4$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $6$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $6$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a67d7d-2e25-5590-abde-d1402ec76c73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345721} {:answer/id #uuid "29f33f9e-9e08-5db0-b36d-be6f1dd9ec29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345724} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9743d4-2101-5a2c-afc8-37f657505898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 1759